## PART 3 · TICKETS (13; create in this order; Summary verbatim)
### Filing rules (B164's, unchanged)
1. **Jira: MPSCALC only, only these rows.** Your own small GET/POST client; `JIRA_BASE_URL`, `JIRA_EMAIL`, `JIRA_API_TOKEN` read BY NAME from `4_Credentials/.env` inside your process: never printed, never on argv, never in a file. Write verbs: `POST /issue`, `POST /issue/{key}/comment`. **No transition, no field edit, no delete, no link, no watcher, no label change on an existing issue.**
2. **Dedupe at write time.** Before EACH create, re-run the row's clause(s) verbatim and `labels = plan-b169-<rid>` (must be 0). Controls once per run: `text ~ "PRE-1"` → drafter 8 (MPSCALC-203, 202, 183, 162, 155, 142, 100, 95); `text ~ "zzqxvbw"` → 0; `created >= "2026-10-17"` → 24 before your first create (MPSCALC-189…212); `labels = mpscalc-b169` → 0. A hit is EXISTING when that ticket's acceptance names the behaviour AND it is not met → comment on it instead of creating (counted). A hit on a met or different acceptance is RELATED: create, and name it. Hits on your own new tickets are separated by `AND labels = mpscalc-b169` and never count. Record every JQL with count and keys.
3. **Shape (B99/B164):** Issue type `Task`. Description ADF, sections `BLUF` · `Recommendation` · `Detail` (Where `file:line @sha` + Symptom) · `Acceptance check` · `Source` (finding ids, `Discovered: during gate Bxxx (2026-10-17)` or `Ruled: <card id> (2026-10-17)`, evidence `1_Project_Definition/Briefs/<STATUS>:<lines>`, related keys). **Assignee:** the board account = MPSCALC-147's assignee `accountId` (GET it; never write the display name). **Labels:** `mpscalc-b169`, `plan-b169-<rid>`, the row's `lane-<x>` / `tier-<n>` / `needs-ruling`. No other new label family. Read each issue back (summary, labels, assignee EQUAL).
4. **No figures** (no price, cost, margin, rate or yield value, synthetic or real), **no person's name** (say "the product owner", "the reviewer"), **no client or customer name**, in any Jira text, label or title. Scan before posting (B164's `scan()`: the client name brief B99's HOLDS line names, the B99 register's "who said it" names, `datasec`, `$`, digit-dot-digit outside shas / versions / `file:line`): 0, with a positive control.

